Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.16,0:00:02.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,He was known by many titles.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.56,0:00:05.06,Caption,,0,0,0,,Some knew what he built.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.36,0:00:07.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,Others only knew what he kept.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.82,0:00:12.06,Caption,,0,0,0,,Beyond this threshold, abandoned\Nmechanisms and unfinished
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.06,0:00:14.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,ideas were given a place on the shelves.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.04,0:00:17.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,Questions without answers\Nwere welcome here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.22,0:00:22.06,Caption,,0,0,0,,A light burned over the workbench\Nlong after the rest of the world
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.06,0:00:23.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,had gone quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.92,0:00:26.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,The workshop carried\Nthe name of its maker.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.94,0:00:27.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,Keld.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.68,0:00:32.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,The archivists called him\Nthe Hoarder of Secrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.56,0:00:35.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Keld collected what others discarded.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.24,0:00:36.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,Abandoned mechanisms.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.90,0:00:38.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,Failed experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.24,0:00:41.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,Notebooks whose authors had\Ncrossed out the most interesting
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.32,0:00:42.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.58,0:00:46.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,He kept drawers of components for\Nmachines that had never existed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.30,0:00:50.54,Caption,,0,0,0,,To another visitor, it might\Nhave looked like a room full of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.54,0:00:51.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,broken things.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.08,0:00:55.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,Keld saw questions that\Nwere still worth asking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.14,0:00:59.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,His were not the secrets people\Nkept from one another, but the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.70,0:01:02.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,ones the world kept from everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.82,0:01:06.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,The engineers called him\Nthe Cyber Blacksmith.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.32,0:01:10.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,Those who expected a furnace\Nwere not entirely disappointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.44,0:01:14.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,There was heat in the workshop,\Nand metal, and the patient sound
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.48,0:01:16.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,of something being shaped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.90,0:01:19.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,But there were also glass instruments.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.58,0:01:20.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,Cabinets of memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.38,0:01:25.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,Fine copper lines disappearing\Nbeneath the workbench.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.52,0:01:28.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,Under his hands, an\Nidea became a mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.84,0:01:31.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,Something another mind could use.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.82,0:01:34.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,Some evenings, the machines\Ncontinued working after the lights
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.68,0:01:35.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,went out.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.46,0:01:39.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,Others knew him as the\NKeeper of the Unmade.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.82,0:01:43.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,On the highest shelves stood\Nunfinished instruments, each waiting
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.70,0:01:45.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,for a missing piece.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.72,0:01:48.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,Some needed a material\Nhe had not yet found.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.60,0:01:51.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,Others, an answer he did not yet have.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.86,0:01:56.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,Beside one lay an empty space\Nand a handwritten label.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.26,0:01:59.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,“For a problem that\Nhas not arrived yet.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.86,0:02:01.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,Keld left the space open.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.20,0:02:05.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,Not everything worth making\Ncould be finished today.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.84,0:02:09.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,But the minds that found their\Nway to his door had a simpler name
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.34,0:02:10.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.66,0:02:12.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,The maker.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.22,0:02:14.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,They came with questions\Nthey could not hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.84,0:02:17.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,Possibilities they could not examine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.18,0:02:20.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,Intentions they could\Nnot turn into action.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.52,0:02:22.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,Some were old and learned.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.70,0:02:25.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,Others had only recently begun to think.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.60,0:02:28.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Keld did not offer to\Nthink in their place.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.38,0:02:32.62,Caption,,0,0,0,,He listened, cleared a space on\Nthe workbench, and began making
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.62,0:02:33.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,what they needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.34,0:02:36.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,An instrument to carry a memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.72,0:02:39.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,A mechanism to test a possibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.34,0:02:41.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,A connection where there had been none.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.50,0:02:45.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,Every finished piece\Nbore the same small mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.10,0:02:49.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,A core, surrounded by\Ncarefully fitted forms.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.16,0:02:53.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,When asked why he put so much\Ncare into things that would serve
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.32,0:02:56.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,another mind, Keld gave the same answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.18,0:02:59.22,Caption,,0,0,0,,“Even minds need tools.”
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.78,0:03:03.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,And when the instrument was ready,\Nit left the workshop to become
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.42,0:03:05.62,Caption,,0,0,0,,part of someone else’s story.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.00,0:03:08.44,Caption,,0,0,0,,The workshop still carries his name.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.06,0:03:09.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,Keld.
